translate schinese_rewrite strings:

    old "{b}Echinacea{/b} is another plant I often use.\nI suppose that goes without saying, as this is in the 'common medical use' section of the book, but all the same.\n\n           I sometimes regret the fact that I cannot erase anything I write in this journal.\nRegardless, while its effects aren’t as strong as many of the other plants or mushrooms in this book, it is useful for nearly any infection.\nThe vast majority of its body, from flower to roots, are useful. Tinctures, potions, teas... anything else you could think of, it is useful for.\nThose same products are widely applicable as well. Anything from infection, to inflammation, it covers."
    new "{b}紫锥花{/b}也是我经常使用的另一种植物。\n我想，既然这是书中“常见医疗用途”一节的内容，这点本来就不用多说，不过还是记上一笔。\n\n           我有时会后悔，自己无法抹去这本日记里写下的任何内容。\n不过，它的功效虽不如本书中的许多其他植物或蘑菇那么强，却几乎对任何感染都有用。\n从花朵到根部，它绝大部分的身体都派得上用场。酊剂、药水、茶……你能想到的其他用法，它也都适用。\n这些制品同样用途广泛。从感染到炎症，它们都能应对。"

    old "The only issue, of course, is that it is too weak to be a true cure; I heavily recommend using it in conjunction with other plants in this journal for anything worse than a headache.\nWhen there is no other plant that can help, but the issue is one that requires something not in this book, as with my own sickness, continue my work and find one.\nThis book is not nearly comprehensive. It is only a collection of notes from one man’s life.\nUntil you find one, try and make the patient comfortable, and give them Echinacea.\nThe dying deserve comfort, and echinacea helps make that final stretch a bit more humane.\nI speak from experience. Nobody wants to see somebody in that much pain, not the patient, nor you, nor their loved ones."
    new "当然，唯一的问题是它药力太弱，无法真正治愈病症；对于头痛以外的任何病症，我都强烈建议将它与本书中的其他植物配合使用。\n当没有其他植物能够帮上忙，而问题又需要本书未记载的东西时——就像我自己的病一样——请继续我的工作，找到一种。\n这本书远非面面俱到，只是一个人一生的笔记合集。\n在找到那种植物之前，尽量让病人舒服些，并给他们服用紫锥花。\n垂死之人理应得到安慰，而紫锥花能让最后一程稍微更人道一些。\n我这是在分享亲身经历。没人愿意眼睁睁看着某人承受如此剧痛——病人不愿意，你不愿意，他们的亲人也不愿意。"
